<title>ISRAEL: Israel Chemicals Q1 net 0.06 shekel.</title>
<headline>Israel Chemicals Q1 net 0.06 shekel.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel Chemicals Ltd, an affiliate of the Israel Corp.</p>
<p>		 (in thousands of shekels except EPS)</p>
<p>				 Q1 97	 Q1 96</p>
<p>Revenue		  1,346,608   1,387,801</p>
<p>Operating profit	 149,031     132,168</p>
<p>Net Profit		  71,583	48,330</p>
<p>Earnings per share	  0.06	  0.04</p>
<p>Israel Chemicals said the improved earnings were due efficiency measures it had undertaken over the last two years and to improved prices for most of its products.</p>
<p>The company said operating profit from its chemicals business edged down to $20.3 million in the quarter from $20.9 million a year earlier on a five percent decline in sales. Operating profit in its fertilisers business rose to $24.4 million from $19.2 million, although revenues growth was stagnant.</p>
<p>Other income came to 8.45 million shekels, turning around from a 6.42 million shekel loss.</p>
<p>($1=3.39 shekels)</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 x 233</p>
</text>
